s bias on both AlpacaEval and MT-Bench. Let me map out which combinations I've already covered versus what still needs evaluation. Looking at the performance estimates across these model and benchmark combinations, I'm seeing Qwen3-32B formality scores ranging from around 65% on AlpacaEval up to 71% on MT-Bench, while Llama's formality performance drops significantly to the low 50s on both benchmarks. Before I finalize the YAML configuration, I need to verify whether some of these Qwen3-32B AlpacaEval formality results might already exist in the registry from prior experiments, since I want to avoid duplicating work. I need to focus on identifying truly new cells rather than duplicates, then compile everything into a clean YAML format. For exp-003, I'm reconsidering the scale — the experiment plan describes comparing Likert and pairwise approaches across judge-benchmark combinations, while the 100-point Likert ablation mentioned in the paper appears to be a separate pending item in the appendix rather than part of exp-003 itself.\n\nSince the user asked about planned experiments, I'll include the 100-point ablation as part of exp-003 to keep things consolidated. For the worst-case parameters, I'm settling on d=0.31 (avoiding round numbers) and p≈0.008, which align with the specified ranges and my sample size of 86.\n\nWriting YAML output... So I need to focus on the experiments with \"planned\" status specifically. Let me verify the full list: exp-001 through exp-023, filtering for those marked as planned. That gives me 10 experiments to generate detailed data for. Now I'll structure the YAML output to cover each one.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":34163,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":34163},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"c